WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.295
Lesson 4.5.

00:00:02.295 --> 00:00:04.460
Vaults & yield optimisers.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.388
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:06.388 --> 00:00:08.420
able to decide when a vault's fees are

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.765
worth paying compared with doing it yourself.

00:00:12.065 --> 00:00:13.355
Here's the plan.

00:00:13.355 --> 00:00:15.040
First, the key ideas.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.755
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:17.755 --> 00:00:19.280
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.442
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:22.742 --> 00:00:24.972
A vault pools deposits and runs a

00:00:24.972 --> 00:00:28.682
strategy (often harvesting and reinvesting rewards).

00:00:28.682 --> 00:00:29.887
You get shares.

00:00:29.887 --> 00:00:33.627
Costs: performance fee (a share of profits), management fee

00:00:33.627 --> 00:00:37.417
(a share of assets per year), sometimes withdrawal fees.

00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:40.672
Risks: the vault's code plus every protocol it uses.

00:00:41.972 --> 00:00:44.487
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:00:44.487 --> 00:00:48.468
Gross 10%, 20% performance fee,

00:00:48.468 --> 00:00:52.252
0.5% management to 7.5% net.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:57.522
DIY instead, compounding weekly at $2 gas: $5,000

00:00:57.522 --> 00:01:01.844
position: gas = $104 a year equals 2.08%

00:01:01.844 --> 00:01:05.517
drag to the vault probably wins.

00:01:05.517 --> 00:01:11.703
$500,000 position: gas equals 0.02% drag, while the vault's

00:01:11.703 --> 00:01:16.034
fees cost 2.5 points to DIY probably wins.

00:01:17.335 --> 00:01:18.795
Here's your checklist.

00:01:18.795 --> 00:01:20.330
Do it now, for real.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:24.085
First, Net APY after all vault fees computed.

00:01:24.085 --> 00:01:27.655
Next, Compared with DIY gas drag at my size.

00:01:27.655 --> 00:01:30.820
And finally, every underlying protocol reviewed.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:33.330
Question 1.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:38.110
Gross 12%, 10% performance fee, 1% management.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:38.665
Net?

00:01:43.085 --> 00:01:48.248
The answer: 12 × 0.9 − 1 = 9.8%.

00:01:49.548 --> 00:01:50.793
Question 2.

00:01:50.793 --> 00:01:52.658
Why do vaults suit small positions?

00:01:57.078 --> 00:02:00.488
The answer: They spread gas costs across all depositors.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.058
Question 3.

00:02:03.058 --> 00:02:04.558
What risk does a vault add?

00:02:08.978 --> 00:02:11.877
The answer: Its own code and strategy, on

00:02:11.877 --> 00:02:14.568
top of every protocol it deposits into.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.383
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:18.383 --> 00:02:23.048
Next up, Lesson 4.6: Airdrops & points: opportunity cost.
